  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+5}{arcsec\\,x}.$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\frac{1}{arcsec\\,x}\\,-$\n\n{{field-2}} \n$\\frac{1}{|x|{arcsec}^{2}\\,x}$",
  "worked_solution": "Here, we let $u(x)={x}^{2}+5$ and $v(x)=arcsec\\,x,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{\u2032}(x)=2x\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x)\\cdot arcsec\\,x-({x}^{2}+5)\\cdot \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}}{(arcsec\\,x)^{2}}. \\\\  & =2x\\,\\frac{1}{arcsec\\,x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}+5}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\frac{1}{|x|{arcsec}^{2}\\,x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
